Faces with N² < −1e-6 s⁻² between vertically adjacent wet cells in the run's initial state
(TEOS-10 as the model, from t = 0 in arctic_ocean.jld2), by region and depth band (0–10, 10–40,
40–200, deeper), with the share of each region's columns that have one; the 15 worst faces with
position, depth, S and T on both sides; maps of the unstable faces in the top 40 m and of the
depth of the shallowest.

Why: the 15 km, 100-level runs start with 56 860 unstable faces, the worst at k = 99 (second
level) with N² ≈ −2.4e-2 s⁻². NEMO's TKE scheme mixes each at 100 m²/s at the first step, and the
melt-lens dipole is already in the first daily mean under ice, with κᶜ at 10–40 m a hundred times
background on day 1.

